## Employment Status

**Consume, don’t rebuild.** The shared `employee.gts` already exports `EmployeeStatusField` (onboarding / active / offboarded) with its color map, plus the sibling `EmployeeEmploymentTypeField` (full-time / part-time / contract / internship). This Spec registers the existing block against the taxonomy row rather than shipping a duplicate enum. A primitive enum cannot carry containedExamples — see the linked Employee (status: active).

### Usage

```ts
import { EmployeeStatusField } from '@cardstack/catalog/cards/hr/employee';

@field status = contains(EmployeeStatusField);
```

`EMPLOYEE_STATUS_COLORS`, exported from the same module, maps each status onto the `StateColor` the pill renders with.

### Non-goals

No new statuses — widening a stored enum forces every consumer’s switch to grow a case; propose additions on the Employee block itself.
